End-to-End Steps for LLM Temperature Demo on AWS EC2
1. Create AWS EC2 Machine

Go to AWS Console → EC2 → Launch Instance

Choose:

AMI: Amazon Linux 2023

Instance type: t3.large (2 vCPU, 8GB RAM)

Key pair: select or create new (download .pem)

Security Group: allow SSH (22)

Launch instance.

Connect via SSH:

ssh -i your-key.pem ec2-user@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>

2. Prepare Environment
sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install -y git curl htop

3. Install Ollama
curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh


Check:

ollama --version

4. Pull a Small Model
ollama pull tinyllama
ollama list


✅ You should see:

tinyllama:latest    <id>    637 MB

5. Create Experiment Script

In your home directory:

cd ~
vi llm_experiment.sh


chmod +x llm_experiment.sh

6. Test Script

Run:

./llm_experiment.sh


Example run:

Enter your prompt: What is DevOps in one line?
Enter temperature (e.g., 0.0, 0.7, 1.2): 0.0
Running with temperature=0.0
